{"availability":"available","full":"game4automation/realvirtual-WEB","name":"realvirtual-WEB","description":"Browser-based 3D-HMI for industrial automation — Three.js/TypeScript viewer for realvirtual digital twins","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":154,"forks":31,"created":"2026-03-26T18:41:59Z","updated":"2026-10-03T10:54:12Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://realvirtual.io","topics":["3d-hmi","digital-twin","industrial-automation","machine-intelligence","plc","threejs","typescript","webgl"],"demo":"https://web.realvirtual.io/demo","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:50.009Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:50.009Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:50.009Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T19:51:50.009Z","stars":154,"forks":31}],"technologies":["React","Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["The browser platform for industrial digital twins — 3D HMI, Machine Information System, simulation and layout planning","realvirtual (formerly realvirtual WEB) is an open-source, browser-based 3D HMI and digital twin platform for manufacturing. Open GLB/glTF models in the browser, simulate drives and material flow, connect machine signals, and build operator dashboards. Simulation components use rvextras metadata, which you can export from realvirtual for Unity Professional or author with your own tools. Viewers need no desktop installation; developers can build the Community application with Node.js.","One link. Any device. Live Digital Twin. Try it: web.realvirtual.io/demo"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/game4automation/realvirtual-WEB/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"9e9323c9b74d30521f37db96d1467816aea5046fdc01530783409f2299cccbd1","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:50.150Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T19:51:50.150Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"The browser platform for industrial digital twins — 3D HMI, Machine Informat